From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 03:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: enable the SM8150 HF AXI bridge

The downstream SM8150 CPAS node enables GCC_CAMERA_HF_AXI_CLK before any
camera client starts.  The mainline port already exposes that clock as
"gcc_camera_axi", but no CAMSS resource requests it, leaving the HF path from
CAMNOC towards memory gated.

This matches the observed failure: VFE0 issues a non-secure write to the exact
buffer IOVA, then CAMNOC reports "Disconnected target" before the transaction
can reach the SMMU.  Enable the HF AXI bridge whenever either full VFE is
powered.  The camera AHB bridge is already critical in GCC and the SF bridge is
not part of the VFE0 RDI0 path under test.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -1357,9 +1357,10 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources vfe_res_8150[] = {
 	/* VFE0 */
 	{
 		.regulators = {},
-		.clock = { "camnoc_axi", "cpas_ahb", "slow_ahb_src",
+		.clock = { "camnoc_axi", "cpas_ahb", "gcc_camera_axi", "slow_ahb_src",
 				"soc_ahb", "vfe0", "vfe0_axi",
 				"vfe0_src", "csi0",
 				"csi0_src" },
 		.clock_rate = { { 0 },
+				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 80000000 },
 				{ 0 },
@@ -1385,9 +1386,10 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources vfe_res_8150[] = {
 	/* VFE1 */
 	{
 		.regulators = {},
-		.clock = { "camnoc_axi", "cpas_ahb", "slow_ahb_src",
+		.clock = { "camnoc_axi", "cpas_ahb", "gcc_camera_axi", "slow_ahb_src",
 				"soc_ahb", "vfe1", "vfe1_axi",
 				"vfe1_src", "csi1",
 				"csi1_src" },
 		.clock_rate = { { 0 },
+				{ 0 },
 				{ 0 },
 				{ 80000000 },
 				{ 0 },
-- 
